{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique","id":1360714,"title":"Build a Spirit (Ephemeral Induction Technique)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-13T11:01:14-08:00","id":1360714,"title":"Build a Spirit (Ephemeral Induction Technique)","content":"So my Solar sorcerer (Essence 3) finally has Ephemeral Induction Technique and wants to create something new and cool. But I'm not sure if we have enough resources on existing spirits to create such a thing. So what I'm looking for is any of the following:<ul><li>What beings have you created with Ephemeral Induction Technique?</li> <li>What stats have you given to homebrewed spirits of any kind?</li> <li>What kinds of spirit powers are out there that you'd recommend choosing or building from?</li> <li>Any other thoughts on this situation?</li> </ul>I'm looking for some advice on how I can make something cool. Certainly I expect a lot of &quot;it depends on what your goal with the spirit is&quot; and I get that, but I'm hoping I'll be inspired by some of what I hear from the forums. <br /> <br /> So let me have it. What cool spirit stuff do you guys have/like/experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T12:00:46-08:00","id":1360726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique#post1360714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What beings have you created with Ephemeral Induction Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, there's <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1km5lUpOk3kH1P-DHdxybY_qirDAc0n_IiOj_nTefBAI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. Of course, I never actually <i>made</i> it, because the game ended not long after, but I did fight and destroy its original form (using the same stats). I don't exactly recall why I statted it the way I did (aside from having actual dots so that it could actually spend its experience), but I do remember specifically going for more health levels than a blood ape, but fewer than a greenmaw.<br /> <br /> I'd build it very differently if I was using EIT today (for one, more mutations to represent the particulars of its shape -- not something you'd need for an NPC spirit).<br /> <br /> The other major spirit I've written is <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N0bx_FQGAal_MGkFVyo7SAkwBkH5L1zAL80hURdTOp4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>, a volcano god for a game I ran in... 2017, I think? He's more of a tangle of Charms and Merits stolen from various parts of the corebook (Incandescent Counter, for instance, is one of Sigereth's Charms). He tested well against an optimized Fire Immaculate (using the <i>A Clutch of Dragons</i> homebrew), but didn't stand up to two Solars.<br /> Me rolling like garbage didn't help.<br /> <br /> Also from that game is a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FuC9b726d8AGS_NPGr6WnNyUumfiftZesyRIsBMIcLA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">half-finished ghost</a>, the spectre of a Dynastic sorceress. A more adventurous design than the volcano god, intended to fight in the flesh of a PC or ally, but she's still mostly cribbed from pre-written material (Flesh That Guards the Dragon was taken from <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/273385/The-Thousand-Sanctioned-Beasts--Elementals\" target=\"_blank\">Thousand Sanctioned Beasts</a>, I believe, and her Passion-Transmuting Nuance is just straight-up the <i>ACoD</i> version).<br /> <br /> So, in summary: I beg, barter and steal; spirits should be weird and flashy; spirit familiars are best familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T12:23:59-08:00","id":1360731,"title":"","content":"In session 0 of my first 3e game my sorcerer used it after finding a tower on an island that was covered in angry spirits of air. He was a really really bad fighter so he used it after caging one of the elementals and using it as a template to make a kind of wind-knight to protect him. I started out using mortal chargen and added a few mutations like wings, and then custom made a small number of charms for things like defend other and eventually a big decisive attack enhancer. Most of the xp went into abilities and attributes though as she grew from a single minded guardian into a more fully developed character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T08:06:20-08:00","id":1361080,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar97_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"97\" data-vbnamecard=\"97\">The MG</a> That's some great examples, thanks for sharing! I'm starting to make a list of all spirit merits, special attacks, and charms listed in the core book to look at for a sampling, but sounds like that's the right direction.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> So you literally built them as a character with xp and such? How did that feel by the end of creation? Were they Essence 1 when you used the Charm? I'm at Essence 3 so we're looking at potentially a different scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T08:39:18-08:00","id":1361085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1361080#post1361080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's some great examples, thanks for sharing! I'm starting to make a list of all spirit merits, special attacks, and charms listed in the core book to look at for a sampling, but sounds like that's the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you have any of the Hundred Devils Night Parade entries, some of them contain good stuff too. Don't be afraid to take raksha Charms, either, though you'll have to increase the mote costs significantly to account for spirit motepools.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, I found another <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NiSVad2R3IH_yWFFJxTD_XeawlJRGnWyiCY_CbMAUE8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">ghost DB</a> among my documents, this time with a bonus hungry ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you literally built them as a character with xp and such? </div> </div> </div> You pretty much have to, since EIT specifies the spirit gains experience. I don't think it would be useful to build it entirely as a player character, but you're pretty much stuck with Attributes and Abilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:33:53-08:00","id":1361120,"title":"","content":"Iirc, since the charm explicitly lets you use chunks of spirits you\u2019ve eaten and captured and everything to help build your new spirit, cribbing directly from the entities you\u2019ve defeated and consumed sounds pretty reasonable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T11:45:22-08:00","id":1361124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1361120#post1361120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, since the charm explicitly lets you use chunks of spirits you\u2019ve eaten and captured and everything to help build your new spirit, cribbing directly from the entities you\u2019ve defeated and consumed sounds pretty reasonable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a key piece of it for me. I haven't actually defeated and consumed any spirits in our travels. Does that invalidate my player ability to copy powers from other spirits when I create this one? Or it's ability to learn similar such powers as it grows and develops?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:13:02-08:00","id":1361130,"title":"","content":"Mechanically? No, that would be silly. Narratively? Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:24:29-08:00","id":1361136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1361080#post1361080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you literally built them as a character with xp and such? How did that feel by the end of creation? Were they Essence 1 when you used the Charm? I'm at Essence 3 so we're looking at potentially a different scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep they were Essence 1. I my backstory for session zero, technically they were created before session 1, I used Carnal Spirit Rending on an air elemental to draw some power forth from it and use as the most basic template for a guardian. Then from then on I got to spend basically double xp every session for myself and my familiar. By the end they were Essence 3 with well rounded stats and a few fairly powerful spirit charms. In the big final climax of that game she managed to fight an entire massive army of hobgoblins on her own so that was pretty solid. Also over the course of that campaign I rarely ever took a hit in spite of having dex 3 and 0-1 in my combat abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:25:31-08:00","id":1361137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1361124#post1361124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a key piece of it for me. I haven't actually defeated and consumed any spirits in our travels. Does that invalidate my player ability to copy powers from other spirits when I create this one? Or it's ability to learn similar such powers as it grows and develops?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it\u2019s ability to learn powers as it develops is just based on its ability to grow in essence and definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:40:27-08:00","id":1361142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1361124#post1361124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a key piece of it for me. I haven't actually defeated and consumed any spirits in our travels. Does that invalidate my player ability to copy powers from other spirits when I create this one? Or it's ability to learn similar such powers as it grows and develops?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having previously consumed spirits might give you a bit more narrative legitimacy, but at the end of the day if your Solar decides they want to create a Spirit which shares traits with multiple existing Spirits there's no reason they can't do it from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T09:32:18-08:00","id":1363463,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be pure spirit or can one take liberties? Because i have a demon[blood ape]-elemental[vaatkri]-ghost[doppelganger]-raksha[cataphract] monster salad made by our group's Twilight out of her sacrficed in battle demon familiar in a previous game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:21:32-08:00","id":1363471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1363463#post1363463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have to be pure spirit or can one take liberties? Because i have a demon[blood ape]-elemental[vaatkri]-ghost[doppelganger]-raksha[cataphract] monster salad made by our group's Twilight out of her sacrficed in battle demon familiar in a previous game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've often wondered the same thing. The charm doesn't specify that it has to fit a specific category, and Ex3 does like to do away a bit less with the categorizing of everything. My instinct is that mixing things up should be kosher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T17:36:01-08:00","id":1363540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360714-build-a-spirit-ephemeral-induction-technique?p=1363471#post1363471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've often wondered the same thing. The charm doesn't specify that it has to fit a specific category, and Ex3 does like to do away a bit less with the categorizing of everything. My instinct is that mixing things up should be kosher.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Overall the text is quite dubious on the subject, it's possible to create spirits from essence drawn from the Solar's surroundings may also use the Essence-patterns of spirits she has captured with Burning Exorcism Technique or absorbed with Carnal Spirit Rending to determine the being\u2019s nature and magic. What in itself is quite interesting as Burning Exorcism Technique deals with &quot;spiritual malaises&quot;, that may cover possession but also curses, diseases imposed by supernatural effects and other undefined stuff.<br /> <br /> How that interfaces or not with the power &quot;to induct a Fair Folk into the world&quot; (that relates with Wyld-Binding Prana), it's up to each ST and at the time me (the player of the recently deceased blood ape familiar) and the Twilight managed to negotiate (she sent him an overpowered mashup of parts, while i offered a more &quot;grounded&quot; combination of some their themes and powers) a peculiar blend of parts that our ST was quite ok with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-28-2020, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}